<p>North Korea’s Naegohyang Women’s FC arrived at Incheon International Airport on Sunday for the AFC Women’s Champions League semifinals, the first visit by North Korean athletes to South Korea in about eight years. South Korea’s Unification Ministry said the delegation included 27 players and 12 staff members. The club is scheduled to play Suwon FC Women on Wednesday in Suwon. In recent years, Pyongyang has described South Korea as its “most hostile state” and ruled out reunification, while South Korean President Lee Jae Myung has called for improved ties. At the airport, civic groups displayed welcome signs, but the players moved quickly to buses under police escort without addressing reporters or supporters.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_41_Fx8pbitCDTOt6KVnz4VHhYmShtJIrU_pT80hDcJ2etZAc5udsgrSD97MYnU6BJomm6VHZ3MziO8sSg2A1A6AP7wJCBQoqYCJFb4_wUUKP6JckRwpcANI5RFQFc99vWKInqCaTDodlWZWO1VrG8g3dE_xv7rtTJ1swEggobYY1fYAu18sCrllpoek2Pol9u2HZ-CSsOCfZWIDcEUD6w' alt='Members of Naegohyang, a North Korean women’s soccer team, arriving at Incheon International Airport in South Korea on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ticket demand: All 7,087 tickets made available to the general public sold out within a day, Yonhap reported, citing South Korea’s football federation.</li><li>Legal approval: Seoul approved the visit under its inter-Korean exchange law for a stay through next weekend, though the team could leave earlier if eliminated.</li><li>Travel route: The delegation left Pyongyang on May 12, trained in Beijing, and then flew to South Korea on an Air China flight, RTHK reported, citing South Korea’s Unification Ministry.</li><li>Post-arrival training: Yonhap reported that Naegohyang reached Suwon after landing and held its first local training session; NoCutNews said the route to the training area was screened off.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>South Korean government officials: Le Figaro reported that Seoul described the match as an opportunity for “mutual understanding” between the two Koreas. (<a href='https://www.lefigaro.fr/sports/football/foot-l-equipe-feminine-nord-coreenne-de-naegohyang-pose-le-pied-en-coree-du-sud-pour-une-rencontre-historique-20260517'>Le Figaro</a>)</li><li>South Korean civic groups: Asiae reported that displaced-family organizations, including Incheon-based groups for people with roots in North Korean provinces, joined other civic groups at the airport welcome. (<a href='https://www.asiae.co.kr/article/2026051718202312891'>Asiae</a>)</li><li>South Korean cheering squad official: A cheering squad official said the visit showed that inter-Korean cooperation was possible in multilateral sports settings. (<a href='https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20260517000300315'>Yonhap News Agency</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The newspaper reported that the team’s trip was unlikely to produce a diplomatic thaw between the two Koreas, while noting that some previous sports events had done so. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/world/asia/north-korea-naegohyang-soccer-football.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/world/asia/north-korea-naegohyang-soccer-football.html'>A North Korean Soccer Team Makes a Rare Visit to South Korea</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3353876/north-korean-footballers-arrive-south-match-tickets-sell-out'>North Korean footballers arrive in South, match tickets sell out</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/17/afc-women-champions-league-north-korea-south-korea-naegohyang-fc-suwon'>‘Tearing down barriers’: North Korean footballers arrive in Seoul for first time in eight years</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/north-korean-womens-soccer-team-arrives-south-korea-133045454'>North Korean women&#x27;s soccer team arrives in South Korea for regional tournament</a> - a